# Keep shell scripts LF-only so a core.autocrlf=true clone does not produce a
# CRLF shebang that fails with a confusing "bad interpreter" error.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The Claude Code skill-port parity check (`.github/scripts/check-claude-skill-ports.sh`)
# compares a committed `diff -u` record against one it recomputes from the two
# skill trees. Under core.autocrlf=true the checked-out record would carry CRLF
# while the recomputed diff does not, so a Windows contributor running the
# check locally as CLAUDE.md documents could never get a green result. Pin all
# three artifacts to LF.
*.diff text eol=lf
.github/skills/** text eol=lf
.claude/skills/** text eol=lf
